  Tiny synchronous envelope/completion-summary reads and occupancy-repair costs remain to measure.
    Transport, final traversal and live selection/view rendering remain later work.

Phase 4 - Traverse stored density and schedule retained work
  Depends on: Phase 3.
  Outcome: bounded ray traversal and fair lighting jobs are ready for both transport solvers.
  [x] Implement the selected initial traversal (coarse DDA unless Phase 1 explicitly revised it),
      retaining state across block boundaries. Support zero direction components, anisotropic cells,
      negative rays, finite edges and circular addressing with forward progress.
  [x] Skip only certified empty support; preserve actual integration lengths and the selected occupied
      sampling rule. Avoid root restarts and silent work-limit truncation of admitted rays.
  [x] Implement separate bounded direct/diffuse queues after density publication. Prioritize new/
      changed content and active/visible stale work, with fair offscreen service and persistent ages.
  [x] Propagate nonlocal density demand conservatively, initially domain-wide if selected. Coalesce
      once per update; retain dirty state and actual completed revisions until successful work.
  [x] Handle light direction, intensity/environment, activation and refinement demand independently.
      Fog/exposure/camera motion must not clear compatible volume history.
  [x] Verify traversal coverage/progress, filter-support safety, fairness/work limits and failed-work
      stamps with focused contract checks. Document behavior; no full performance matrix here.
  [x] Completion: traversal is bounded and conservative, and queued work cannot become falsely fresh
      through selection alone or indefinitely starve due to repeated content changes.

