Phase 6 - Progressively transport diffuse illumination
  Depends on: Phase 5.
  Outcome: retained higher-order/environment source is refined under a fixed budget.
  [x] Implement the specified recurrence using stored density/direct visibility and previous diffuse
      source; physical segment extinction/albedo and normalized direction weights govern transport.
  [x] Include incoming environment once, traverse empty gaps, and keep outgoing first scattering
      separate from diffuse higher orders. Use selected finite radiance bounds/encoding.
  [x] Copy published diffuse data to the destination before partial writes; preserve untouched values,
      perform selected updates from the coherent source, then publish field and scale together.
      Skip copy/swap for empty batches. Charge copy traffic separately from solver work. Phase 7.6
      supersedes the original full-copy implementation with bounded repair and scale-safe fallback.
  [x] Propagate refinement demand and retain stale illumination across ordinary atmosphere changes.
      Apply the agreed fallback/transition policy without mixing incompatible density identities.
  [x] Verify declared recurrence/units, bounds, copy preservation, scale publication and failure rules
      with focused tests only; no convergence or reference-image threshold. Update current docs.
  [x] Completion: bounded successful batches refine a coherent persistent source without double
      counting environment/first scattering or losing untouched regions.

