Phase 7.2 - Remove intermediate frame waits from retained volume updates
  Depends on: Phase 7.1.
  Outcome: dependent GPU stages execute as one bounded update chain where possible, while rendering
    retains the last completed publication. Intermediate CPU decisions no longer impose avoidable
    render-frame boundaries or reduce the frequency of useful lighting work.
  [x] Record a narrow current baseline using the corrected traversal: callbacks and elapsed frames
      per publication, useful direct/diffuse jobs per rendered frame, backlog/completion age, CPU
      readbacks and per-stage/total GPU cost. Include unchanged and evolving weather, source changes
      and empty batches. Do not reuse timings from the undersampling traversal as a matched baseline.
  [x] Audit CloudVolumeUpdates, CloudVolumeDensity, CloudVolumeWork and CloudVolumeDiffuse dependencies.
      Separate CPU-required admission/domain decisions from GPU producer-consumer ordering. Identify
      each fence/readback and why it is needed; retain asynchronous admission where CPU results are
      necessary without turning every downstream stage into a separate rendered-frame step.
  [x] Chain work selection, direct tracing/completion and diffuse copy/gather/completion through the
      existing command stream with explicit storage/image/texture/indirect-command barriers. Include
      density generation/occupancy in that chain wherever its validated admission permits. Remove
      intermediate fences used only to sequence GPU consumers; do not imply backend async-compute
      overlap or move graphics commands to an unsupported CPU thread/context.
  [x] Remove the intermediate CPU diffuse-job-count decision. Use GPU-produced counts/conditional
      work to suppress empty tracing and unnecessary whole-field copying, while preserving coherent
      old-field reads, untouched texels, encoding/scale compatibility and correct swap/publication
      semantics. Do not swap in an uninitialized destination when GPU-selected work is empty.
  [x] Accumulate arithmetic/completion status on the GPU and inspect it after the final completion
      fence. Poll with zero timeout on later frames; no ordinary-play waits, immediate buffer maps,
      spin loops or fixed frame delays. Failed work must not publish fields, encoding or completion
      claims as successful. Retain CPU validation before decisions that genuinely require it.
  [x] Simplify the scheduler around bounded pending updates and completed publications. Submit the
      next eligible chain promptly after the previous chain retires, without an artificial idle
      frame. Preserve frozen inputs, coalesced newer weather, executable/context certificates,
      ownership, recenter/replacement/reconfiguration cancellation and safe resource reuse.
      Keep current ray schedules, directions, texture resolution, 4096/64/32 work budgets and memory
      ceilings; improve submission cadence instead of hiding the issue by increasing budgets.
  [x] Extend only affected existing ordering, empty-work, failure/publication and lifecycle checks
      through actual GPU/program/binding abstractions. Verify coherent publication, successful-only
      stamps, no intermediate CPU waits and unchanged bounded work. No approximation-quality, image
      difference or convergence gates, redundant fixtures or broad test matrix.
  [x] Use subagents for focused incremental builds/tests. Reuse passing evidence during iteration;
      no routine clean builds, full baseline reproduction or packaging. Repeat only the matched
      throughput measurements needed to evaluate changed candidates; final qualification remains
      Phase 9. State contention and distinguish GPU execution time from frame-level update latency.
  [x] Reconcile the proposal's Nonblocking updates and drawable publication contract and current
      PBR.Clouds.md architecture with delivered ordering, status handling and resource accounting.
      Record any remaining CPU admission boundary or throughput limitation explicitly.
  [x] Completion: avoidable intermediate frame boundaries/readbacks are removed, useful update
      throughput and publication latency have matched before/after evidence at unchanged budgets,
      and drawable isolation, bounded work and failure/lifecycle contracts remain intact. No live
      FPS or appearance acceptance is inferred from focused checks.

