Phase 8.2 evaluation and rejection
  Support/safety -> proposal / Traversal acceleration candidates, Initial acceleration selection,
    Native inputs and coordinate identity -> tested capped integer block-distance relaxation from
    conservative occupancy. Distance zero included entire occupied cell boxes and occupancy halo.
    Eight 26-neighbor relaxations capped Chebyshev block distance at eight; X/Z wrapped, vertical
    exterior acted as occupied. Distance d certified the block-index cube of radius d-1 empty.
    Distance to its nearest face defines a conservative unsigned physical-distance bound; the tested
    lookup used the stronger directional ray exit in metres. This was not a Euclidean distance texture.
    Original-ray integer planes accounted for anisotropy, partial seam blocks and finite clipping;
    stepping stayed one float below the computed cube exit and resumed unchanged exact voxel DDA.
  Memory -> proposal / Layout and memory limits -> prototype appended two uint/block slices to each
    working occupancy buffer and one to drawable occupancy, plus twelve header bytes per buffer.
    Maximum additional working574612bytes, drawable287312, replacement1436536; peak1035387288
    remained below1073741824. A working slice was construction scratch; no per-voxel volume/spare.
    These are owned payload calculations, not driver allocation measurements. All were removed.
  Updates/publication -> proposal / Nonblocking updates and drawable publication; PBR.Clouds.md /
