Phase 8.2 retry - physical block-distance lookup
  User requested another attempt on2026-10-21. Replaced capped cube exits with three separable
    min/max transforms of physical block-box gaps. Weighted L-infinity distance conservatively
    bounded Euclidean separation from every point of a block to potentially occupied support.
    X/Z used circular physical gaps including short blocks; Y had no artificial exterior seeds.
    Scalar lookup retained original-ray float/direction allowances and finite clipping.
  Tested three lookup revisions: scalar jumps with DDA reinitialization; distance-only empty state
    deferring fine planes until support; and final distances packed into occupancy's upper16bits.
    Packed half-metre units rounded down and saturated at32767.5m; low bits retained occupancy/repair.
    Zero/short bounds returned before separate metadata loads and position arithmetic. This removed
    the extra distance fetch. Working scratch added574612bytes, final drawable header only12bytes;
    combined replacement increment1149236bytes stayed below the existing1GiB ceiling. All removed.
  Source traceability remains proposal / Traversal acceleration candidates, Native inputs and
    coordinate identity, Layout and memory limits, Nonblocking updates and drawable publication;
    inherited Clouds/Atmosphere/Enablement contracts are unchanged. No settings or budgets changed.
  Existing fixtures compared515x66x515 fields at3440x1377/quarter tracing, sparse and denser layers,
    all three consumers, ABBA order and same-domain construction. These were authored fields at the
    captured allocation size, not replayed captured weather. No approximation or speed thresholds.
    Initial6checks passed; retained-state and packed revisions each passed3affected checks. Corrected
    two initially out-of-band oracle rays before final validation:8occupied samples before support
    addition and16afterward remained identical; operations28->15/16 and35->28/29. CPU box-gap and
    downward quantization assertions covered anisotropy, circular seams and short blocks.
  Final packed ABBA medians: sparse view DDA1.4029/1.4172ms versus distance1.4397/1.4162ms (overlap);
    denser view DDA1.1919/1.1858 versus distance1.2421/1.2421ms (about4%slower). Sparse direct tied
    at.0123ms and diffuse tied at.0358ms. Construction added about.0307ms at the same allocation.
    Retaining empty state reduced the scalar retry's regression but did not establish total benefit.
    Timing includes the actual view/reconstruction path; uncontrolled contention remains a limitation.
  Decision: reject this retry too. Restored all renderer/test sources to the approved DDA content;
